    "body": "The P2WPKH inputs in BIP-375's test vectors cannot be spent by the keys they carry, and none of the 42 signatures in the vectors verifies. Each P2WPKH program is `SHA256(pubkey)[:20]` instead of `HASH160(pubkey)`, and the reference validator does not check signatures, so no test catches it.\n\nThis PR repairs the file in place. Each P2WPKH program becomes `HASH160(pubkey)`. The signatures are re-made with RFC 6979 and low S, under BIP 143 for P2WPKH and P2SH-P2WPKH and under the legacy sighash for P2PKH and the bare input. The `SIGHASH_NONE` vector now has a `SIGHASH_NONE` signature, as BIP 174 requires. The two signatures with no defined sighash, on the segwit v2 input and in the vector missing `PSBT_OUT_SCRIPT`, are removed; both vectors still fail for the same reason. The other 40 signatures now verify, and the runner's `-vv` output is unchanged: 43 passed. I did not regenerate the file, because that would also change unrelated values such as the prevout txids.\n\n#2317, which depends on this PR, makes the test runner check these signatures: on master's vectors it reports 39 of 43 failing, on this PR's none. #2256 and #2207 edit some of the same vectors, and their P2WPKH inputs have the same defect. Whichever of this PR and #2256 lands second needs a rebase and the same repair.\n\n*Made with my usual tools: a computer, the Internet and an LLM. The mistakes, as usual, are all mine.*\n",
